// When the caller asks for unoptimized output, nested function bodies must also
// be raw, otherwise debug and inspection callers would silently see optimized
// bytecode inside the constants table. Raw, `f`'s body for `1;` is `Constant;
// Pop` followed by the implicit unit `Return`; optimized, the peephole drops
// the leading `Constant; Pop`.
// compile: analysed, analysed optimized
fn f() { 1; }
